WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.880
“Fruits and Vegetables Put
to the Test for Boosting Mood”

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.240
There are two components of
psychological health: the absence

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.360
of mental health disorders
such as depression, as well as

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.720
the existence of positive
psychological well-being.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.080
That's the focus of an emerging
field of positive psychology

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.840
focusing on happiness, life
satisfaction, and flourishing,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.040
which may translate to physical
benefits such as improvements

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.200
in blood pressure, immune
function, and longevity.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.560
What is the contribution of food
consumption to well-being?

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.280
Well, studies have linked the
consumption of fruits and vegetables

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.440
with enhanced well-being. A systematic
review of research found evidence

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.920
that consuming fruits and
vegetables was associated with

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:53.600
increased psychological well-being.
Okay, but that's just an association.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.600
A famous criticism in this area of
research is that maybe there's just

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.520
some inherent personality trait
or type of family upbringing

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.000
that might lead people simultaneously

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.160
to eat in a healthy way, and also
to have better mental well-being.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.400
So the diet is merely correlated
with, but incorrectly gives

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.400
the appearance of helping to
cause the level of well-being.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.520
But recent research circumvented
this problem by seeing

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.560
if changes in diet are correlated
with changes in mental well-being,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.840
in effect studying the evolution
of well-being and happiness

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.520
after increases in the consumption
of fruits and vegetables.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.400
And look at that graph—a straight-line
increase between how much more fruits

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.280
and veggies people started eating
and their change in life satisfaction

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.760
over time. Increased fruit and
vegetable consumption appeared

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.080
predictive of increased happiness,
life satisfaction, and well-being—

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.560
up to 0.24 life-satisfaction points for
an increase of eight portions a day.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.920
What does that mean?
Is that a lot? Is that a little?

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.080
That's a lot, equal in size
to the psychological gain

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.080
of going from unemployed
to getting a job.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.680
My Daily Dozen recommendation
is for at least nine servings

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.080
of fruits and veggies a day.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.320
This study was done in Australia.
It was repeated in the UK, and

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.080
researchers there found the same
thing, though the Brits may need

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.320
to bump up their daily minimum to
more like 10 or 11 servings a day.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.640
Okay, but does eating fruits and veggies
also reduce the risk of depression

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.960
and anxiety? I mean
well-being is nice,

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.160
but governments and medical
authorities are often interested

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.160
in the determinants of major
mental illness, not life satisfaction.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:45.040
And indeed, using the same data set
but instead looking for mental illness,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.320
eating fruits and vegetables may
help to protect against future risk

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:52.080
of clinical depression
and anxiety as well.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.000
A systematic review and meta-
analysis of dozens of studies found

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:02.160
that every 100-gram increased intake of
fruit was associated with a 3% reduced

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:08.000
risk of depression. That's about
half an apple, yet less than 10%

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.480
of most Western populations
even consume a bare minimum.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.160
Maybe the problem is we're just telling
people about the long-term benefits

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.880
of fruit intake for chronic
disease prevention,

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.640
rather than the near-immediate
improvements in well-being.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.400
So maybe we should be advertising
the happiness gains,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.240
but first we need to
make sure they're real.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:36.000
We've been talking about associations.
Yes, a healthy diet may reduce the risk

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.760
of future depression or anxiety, but
being diagnosed with depression

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.200
or anxiety today could also lead
to lower fruit and vegetable intake.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.560
Now, in these studies you can
indeed show that the increase in fruit

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:53.040
and vegetable consumption came
first, and not the other way around,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.320
but as the great enlightenment
philosopher pointed out,

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.040
just because the cock
crows before the dawn

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.160
doesn't mean the cock
caused the sun to rise.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.480
To prove cause-and-effect

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.880
you need to put it to the test
with an interventional study.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.760
Unfortunately, to date many
studies were like this,

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.920
where those randomized to eat fruit
showed significant improvements

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.080
in anxiety and depression, fatigue,
and emotional distress.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:27.200
Wow, amazing! But that was compared
to chocolate and potato chips.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.080
Apples, clementines, and bananas
making people feel better than assorted

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:38.000
potato chips and chunky chocolate
wafers—not exactly a revelation.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.600
This is the kind of study I've been
waiting for: a randomized controlled

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:46.720
trial in which young adults were
randomized to a diet-as-usual group,

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.040
encouragement to eat
more fruits and veggies,

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.880
or a third group given two servings
of fruits and vegetables a day

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.760
to eat over and above
their regular diet.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.960
And the ones given fruits and
veggies showed improvements

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.720
in their psychological well-being
with increases in vitality, flourishing,

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:06.320
and motivation within just two weeks!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.920
However, simply educating people
to eat their fruits and vegetables

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.040
may not be enough
to reap the full rewards,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.880
so perhaps greater emphasis needs to
be placed on actually providing people

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:21.680
with fresh produce, for example, offering
free fruit for people when they shop.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:25.101
I know that would certainly
make me happy!

